# If it weren't for you in Russian: если бы не, без вас, а то
subtitle: "Если бы не вы, без вас я бы не справилась, ешьте, а то…: conditions without если, as Tom looks after Нина Петровна and she gives him her mother's recipes."
tags: ["russian","если бы не","russian conditional","а то иначе","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/conditionals","vocabulary/body"]
thumb: "band \"If it weren't for you\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}

## If it weren't for you in Russian: если бы не, без вас, а то
stress: new
